    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "148a8c223c804f17927dc122446a3dd9b0cc21d3ed83b1fd4bf43fb8516d063d",
      "text": "Day 5 · An early start to see the sunrise at the El Tatio Geysers, over 4,000 m, one of the most important geothermal fields in the world: more than 70 fumaroles send up jets of steam against the deep blue sky. Breakfast amid the geysers (temperatures can reach 25 °C by day but fall to −2 °C at dawn), then a bath in a natural thermal pool. On the way back, look out for vicuñas and viscachas, and stop at Machuca, a tiny Atacameño village of adobe and cactus-wood houses, with its church of San Santiago and a small wetland home to flamingos. Transfer to Calama for your flight to Santiago, and transfer to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1nHB-5Xavr6R_fNkR408Fk_Ch8G6c2l00",
        "documentSha256": "f30e74c88d9ecd8c21cebe8c69f0e733dd98d406ac3056d25ae9d00ef819452c",
